{"name":"Eros Pink","hex":"#c84f68","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eros","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A winged figure of a child representing love or its power.","Physical love; sexual desire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eros"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eros","blocks":[{"text":"Eros is the Greek god of love and sex. The Romans referred to him as Cupid or Amor. In the earliest account, he is a primordial god, while in later accounts he is the child of Aphrodite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Eros_Farnese_N%C3%A1poles_05.jpg/330px-Eros_Farnese_N%C3%A1poles_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eros","wikidata":"Q121973"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Catalogue_of_the_bronzes%2C_Greek%2C_Roman%2C_and_Etruscan%2C_in_the_Department_of_Greek_and_Roman_Antiquities%2C_British_Museum_%281899%29_%2814783769792%29.jpg/500px-Catalogue_of_the_bronzes%2C_Greek%2C_Roman%2C